# program: fixtures/FX-demo-lamp-tone-1/lamp-tone.listing.txt (ivs-demo-lamp-tone-1), entered through the
#   project boot stub contract 2 (boot-stub-2: cartridge reset entry 5000, interrupt entry 5004), with
#   the zero graphics ROM and no EXEC image
#
# Predicate of ivs-demo-lamp-tone-1 under the six scripted controller events of
# data/scenarios/demo-lamp-tone-pass.ivss (plan 07-07, D-04, D-05, D-21, D-22, D-23, A-02, A-05, A-16): the
# guest memory words at four run-to bounds, the delivered frames, the PSG write log and the raw sample
# levels, all derived by hand in docs/video/demo-lamp-tone-1-derivation.md (sections (c) to (f); the
# frame literals data/video/frames/F-S1.frame to F-S6.frame with their sha256-text keys) BEFORE the
# program, its listing, the scenario or any run existed (oracle commit 4e0febef675c2e81fe38d6c0caf353625218b1eb, then
# the blind second-read record), and copied here line for line from the committed assert block. It was
# not generated by, read back from or edited to match the core or a run. The author of this derivation also
# wrote the literals, the STIC and PSG rules, the program and the core, so all of them can share one
# misreading of a source; agreement among them is not independent evidence about hardware. The controller
# byte table, the STIC rules and the PSG rules are tier 4 or inference, so a claim that rests on this file
# is only as strong as its weakest field and stays provisional.
# Progress, not a title screen: the guest words (marker 03C5, the frame counter floor(T / 59,736) at each
# bound, per port the last byte and the change counter) are asserted at all four steps together with
# halted == no, the displayed flags, six frame hashes tied to F-S1 to F-S6 and pixel probes inside and
# outside the lamp rectangles, the PSG write log by address, value and source (never by tick), and the
# sample levels only at ticks where the level is exact (silence before the first gate write, A=0 B=0 C=15
# in the gate window, silence after the release).
# Excluded on purpose: machine time (printed in the report, never asserted), all CPU registers, R7 and
# the flags (C40, C45, C56), the stack word [0340] (C68), the exact duration of the interrupt service
# routine and the re-arm delay (only the derived bounds are used, through the frame counter and the
# displayed flags), the tick of a log record, and the tone phase (no sample inside a tone window is
# asserted).
# Body: one assert per clause in the runner's scenario grammar, hex upper case, exact compare, evaluated
# at the end of the step above it, in the order of data/scenarios/demo-lamp-tone-pass.ivss
# (golden-expect-drift). The step lines below are comments.
